---
import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import SoftCta from '../components/SoftCta.astro';
import { blogPostsByDateAsc } from '../data/blog';

// The origin-story series, oldest → newest (part one → the latest chapter).
const journalPosts = blogPostsByDateAsc;
const partWords = ['one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six'];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Jacob Vermeulen — Songdance"
  description="Jacob Vermeulen — pianist, singer, and educator, and the person behind Somatic Vocal Healing. He holds space; people heal themselves."
  image="/media/library/jacob-sunset.webp"
  imageAlt="Jacob Vermeulen in the mountains at sunset."
>
  <header class="sd-section sd-about-hero">
    <div class="sd-about-hero-inner">
      <figure class="sd-about-portrait">
        <img src="/media/library/jacob-tree.webp" alt="Jacob Vermeulen" />
      </figure>
      <div class="sd-about-intro" data-anim="reveal">
        <div class="sd-eyebrow">About</div>
        <h1 class="sd-pagehero-title">Jacob Vermeulen</h1>
        <p class="sd-pagehero-lede">
          Founder of Somatic Vocal Healing. Pianist, singer, and educator.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p>
        I started with singing. For nearly ten years I taught authentic singing
        — holidays, workshops, retreats — fascinated less by technique than by something
        underneath it: change how a person <em>feels</em>, and the voice changes on its own. The
        reverse turned out to be true too. That was the question I kept following.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then life did what life does. My late wife, Upala, as she lost her speech to illness,
        started to sound — before any of this was a method, before it had a name. She used it to
        acknowledge her own feelings, and each time she did, she’d move from turmoil to something
        like bliss in a couple of minutes. I had never seen anything like it in my whole career
        as a singer.
      </p>
      <p>
        So my focus moved from singing to sounding — from the voice that reaches for something
        beautiful to the voice that tells the truth about what’s happening inside, in this exact
        moment. Both are real; I simply followed the second one. Out of that, over years and a
        great many sessions, Somatic Vocal Healing took shape.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am a teacher and I hold space; people heal themselves. My job is to
        make that safe and possible, and then to step back. I’ve had the privilege of
        doing this with thousands of people across Europe and South Africa, online and in person
        — and I’m still learning what the voice can do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-about-quote">
    <p class="t-lyric sd-about-quote-text">
      “Don’t expect miracles — expect a real relationship with your own voice.”
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p>
        Songdance is the home for this work — the name for everything that has grown around it:
        the workshops and retreats, the twelve-week course, the online sessions, the
        <a href="/courses/songdeck">Songdeck</a> and its app, and the people who keep returning to sound
        together. It began as a way to gather what I was teaching in one place, and it has become
        a close, safe, and supportive community across Europe and South Africa, in person and
        online, held by a handful of teachers I trust.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-about-journal">
    <div class="sd-about-journal-inner">
      <div class="sd-eyebrow">The story behind it</div>
      <h2 class="sd-about-journal-title">How it all began — in three parts.</h2>
      <p class="sd-about-journal-lede">
        The longer version — Upala, the journeys we made together, and what grew from the loss —
        lives in the Journal.
      </p>
      <ol class="sd-about-journal-list">
        {
          journalPosts.map((post, i) => (
            <li class="sd-about-journal-item">
              <a href={post.href}>
                <span class="sd-about-journal-part">Part {partWords[i] ?? String(i + 1)}</span>
                <span class="sd-about-journal-text">
                  <span class="sd-about-journal-t">{post.title}</span>
                  <span class="sd-about-journal-x">{post.excerpt}</span>
                </span>
                <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true" />
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <a class="sd-about-journal-all" href="/blog">
        All journal entries <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sd-section sd-prose">
    <div class="sd-prose-inner">
      <p class="sd-about-facts">
        Jacob lives in Belgium with his partner, Lieselot, and their son, Pepe. He works in English; the
        German-language practice is led by <strong>Carmen &amp; Lorenz</strong>, and he
        collaborates with <strong>Karen Evans</strong>, <strong>Daniela Hess</strong>, and
        <strong>Lesanne</strong> across courses and retreats.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SoftCta
    text="Curious how this actually feels?"
    ctaLabel="Try a live workshop — 22€"
    ctaHref="/workshop"
    altLabel="What is SVH? →"
    altHref="/what-is-svh"
  />
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* "The story behind it" — the three-part origin story, linked from the Journal. */
  .sd-about-journal-inner {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--t-h2);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: var(--sp-4) 0 var(--sp-6);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--sp-5);
    padding: var(--sp-5) var(--sp-2);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item a:hover {
    background: var(--paper-deep);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-part {
    flex: none;
    width: 5.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-caption);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    padding-top: 0.35em;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-text {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-t {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item a:hover .sd-about-journal-t {
    color: var(--ember-deep);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-x {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item a > i {
    flex: none;
    align-self: center;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    transition:
      transform var(--d-base) var(--ease),
      color var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-item a:hover > i {
    color: var(--ember-deep);
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-all {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: var(--sp-6);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .sd-about-journal-all:hover {
    color: var(--ember-deep);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-all i {
    font-size: 15px;
    transition: transform var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .sd-about-journal-all:hover i {
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .sd-about-journal-item a {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-4);
    }
    .sd-about-journal-part {
      width: auto;
      padding-top: 0;
    }
    .sd-about-journal-item a > i {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
